1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,300
A ticket arrives. You need more than a label. You need the
right action, and a recorded result.

2
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:15,442
Charged twice. System One selects payments. Pi runs the
assignment tool and records the outcome.

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,675
Now change the ticket. Payment failed, and the service is
down. This needs more evidence.

4
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:30,258
When enabled, System One asks System Two to investigate,
using only the tools you permit.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,875
The helper checks the order and service status, then returns
evidence of an outage.

6
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:45,558
System One uses that evidence to choose SOS. Pi assigns the
ticket and records the result.

7
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:58,450
Turbo connects the flow. You supply the policy and relevant
state. Keep your Pi extensions and MCP tools. Fast judgments
drive. Deeper reasoning helps when needed.
